JPEG-in-JXL Lossless Recompression — session-final bench (2026-05-28)
=====================================================================

Bench at main = a53c9c46 (after all session chunks landed).

Sample: 200 JPEGs (66 baseline + 134 progressive) drawn from
`/home/lilith/product-images` + `/home/lilith/work/codec-corpus` via
`random.seed(11)`. Stratified to match the ~33/67 baseline/progressive
split observed in the corpus via file(1).

Encoders:
- cjxl: libjxl v0.12.0 4279d48 (`/home/lilith/work/jxl-efforts/libjxl/build/tools/cjxl`)
- ours: `cjxl-rs` (this repo, --no-default-features --features
  'jpeg-reencoding,parallel,jxl_encoder/std')

Roundtrip verification: djxl v0.12.0 d2c7032 `--reconstruct_jpeg` via
extension auto-detect.

Result:
- Roundtrip OK:    200 / 200 (100%)
- Roundtrip DIFF:  0   / 200
- Encode failed:   0   / 200
- Source total:    54,772,394 bytes
- cjxl total:      44,802,893 bytes  (81.85% of src)
- ours total:      45,484,995 bytes  (83.10% of src)
- Δ vs cjxl:       +1.522%

Session trajectory (commits on origin/main, chronological):
