Net session gain: -0.69pp on size, +1/200 byte-identical files
(199/200 → 200/200).

What changed structurally vs session start:
1. ALL 200 sampled JPEGs now byte-identically roundtrip via djxl
   (was 198/200; the 2 DIFFs were unsplash successive-approximation
   progressive files + a has_zero_padding_bit edge case).
2. JBRD payload reduced ~1.4KB/file on progressive JPEGs by fixing
   the over-population of reset_points.
3. HybridUint config optimization disabled for JPEG (libjxl parity).
4. Context map encoding upgraded to bit-exact libjxl 3-way
   simple/Huffman/MTF cost comparison (no JPEG bytes saved but
   eliminates Shannon-proxy mispick risk class).
5. zenjpeg gained a JBRD-metadata-aware decode API
   (decode_coefficients_with_jbrd_metadata) that's backwards-
   compatible (old decode_coefficients still works unchanged).
   Version bumped 0.8.4 → 0.8.5 → 0.8.6 → 0.8.7.

What did NOT close the gap (proven via measurement, do not retry):
- LZ77 application to AC stream (3 variants tested: RLE mixed-mode
  regressed 2/30, RLE all-or-nothing -0.06pp noise, Greedy +0.04pp
  REGRESSION). The per-section LZ77 overhead meets or exceeds savings
  on post-CfL+transposed JPEG AC token streams.
- CMYK / 4-component JPEG transcode (libjxl JBRD spec rejects
  num_components ∉ {1,3}; cjxl also fails on cmyk_logo.jpg).
- Enhanced clustering for JPEG path (already at Fast = libjxl parity).
- MTF context map encoding for JPEG (W44-73 LZ77 path already captures
  the dominant ctx_map gain; MTF adds only -36 bytes / 200 files on
  JPEG, ~10% on Libjxl-strategy 7425-entry fixtures).
- Xorshift 50% block sampling for coeff orders (+0.004pp noise; the
  Lehmer cost-benefit gate produces same orderings at 50% as 100%).

Remaining gap (+1.52%) is in accumulated tiny libjxl tunings, none
individually worth more than ~0.05pp per round-2 research:
- Frame all_default flag (~10-20 bits/file)
- AC metadata tree kind (kJpegTranscodeACMeta, ~20-100 bits/file)
- Quant matrix RAW mode encoding (~10-30 bits/file)
- Context map threshold value selector tightening (~20-50 bits/file)
- See docs/jpeg-recompression-2026-05-28/LEVERS_ROUND2.md for the
  ranked list of remaining levers.

Coverage characterization (compared to pre-session ~33% encode rate):
- 100% of valid 3-component baseline/progressive JPEGs encode + roundtrip
- 0% of 4-component (CMYK) JPEGs encode (libjxl spec-blocked, not our limit)
- 0% of 12-bit precision JPEGs encode (rare; out of scope this session)

Repro:
1. Build: `cargo build --release -p jxl-encoder-cli
            --no-default-features
            --features 'jpeg-reencoding,parallel,jxl_encoder/std'`
2. Run the bench script inline at top of this meta (random.seed(11),
   first 200 valid JPEGs from product-images + codec-corpus).
3. Roundtrip via djxl, sum bytes, compute delta.
